cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite the paper."
title: "Feedback That Backfires: Why Small Language Model Agents Repeat the Call They Just Watched Fail"
authors:
  - family-names: Gumaan
    given-names: Esmail
repository-code: "https://github.com/Esmail-ibraheem/feedback-that-backfires"
url: "https://github.com/Esmail-ibraheem/feedback-that-backfires"
abstract: >-
  Agent harnesses record a failed tool call and its error message in the
  transcript on the assumption that the error is corrective. We measure the
  corrective gain of a failure record and find it negative across five
  instruction-tuned models (135M-1.2B, four families) in two environments.
  Counterfactual observations show the damage is carried by the failed call's
  surface form rather than by the model misreading the error, which localises
  the problem in the harness and predicts which remedies work.
keywords:
  - language model agents
  - small language models
  - tool use
  - agent harness
  - execution feedback
  - constrained decoding
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-08-09"
